1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,613
At the airport, the boxes

2
00:00:02,613 --> 00:00:04,280
don't board one by one.

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,052
They're packed into these.

4
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:10,456
Containers shaped to fit the

5
00:00:10,456 --> 00:00:11,796
inside of the plane.

6
00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:19,772
But the plane isn't flying to mom's city.

7
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:23,084
It's flying to Louisville, Kentucky.

8
00:00:23,984 --> 00:00:25,479
And so are planes from all

9
00:00:25,479 --> 00:00:26,456
over the country.

10
00:00:27,606 --> 00:00:29,518
Louisville is within a four-hour

11
00:00:29,518 --> 00:00:31,669
flight of ninety-five percent of the

12
00:00:31,669 --> 00:00:33,342
people in the United States.

13
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:35,706
That's not an accident.

14
00:00:36,006 --> 00:00:37,878
That's why the hub is here.

15
00:00:39,228 --> 00:00:42,132
Late at night, planes line up in the dark.

16
00:00:43,182 --> 00:00:45,498
At the busiest moments, about

17
00:00:45,498 --> 00:00:47,334
one lands every minute.

18
00:00:49,534 --> 00:00:51,406
This is Worldport.

19
00:00:51,706 --> 00:00:53,770
UPS's main air hub.

20
00:00:54,570 --> 00:00:56,922
Five point two million square feet.

21
00:00:57,822 --> 00:01:00,174
Roughly ninety football fields,

22
00:01:00,474 --> 00:01:02,346
under one roof.

23
00:01:04,896 --> 00:01:07,272
Some planes don't even stop on the ramp.

24
00:01:08,172 --> 00:01:09,815
They pull right up to the

25
00:01:09,815 --> 00:01:11,196
building, nose first,

26
00:01:11,496 --> 00:01:13,416
like a car into a garage.

27
00:01:14,966 --> 00:01:16,838
The containers come off,

28
00:01:17,138 --> 00:01:19,010
the doors open,

29
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,200
and the boxes go onto belts.

30
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:23,318
Small boxes,

31
00:01:23,618 --> 00:01:25,490
big boxes,

32
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:27,451
and weird-shaped ones each

33
00:01:27,451 --> 00:01:28,738
get their own lane.

34
00:01:32,138 --> 00:01:34,579
Then they pass through tunnels of cameras

35
00:01:34,579 --> 00:01:36,722
that read the label from every side.

36
00:01:37,622 --> 00:01:39,494
Nobody opens your box.

37
00:01:39,794 --> 00:01:41,666
Nobody even looks at it.

38
00:01:42,816 --> 00:01:45,075
The system reads the address, picks

39
00:01:45,075 --> 00:01:47,270
the right plane, and starts moving

40
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:48,432
the box toward it.

41
00:01:49,332 --> 00:01:51,379
There are more than a hundred and fifty

42
00:01:51,379 --> 00:01:53,532
miles of conveyor belts in this building.

43
00:01:54,482 --> 00:01:56,954
ZERO decides to follow his box.

44
00:01:59,182 --> 00:02:01,342
ZERO does not follow his box.

45
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:07,356
But the system never loses it.

46
00:02:08,256 --> 00:02:10,224
Every scan updates where it is,

47
00:02:10,524 --> 00:02:12,804
even when ZERO has no idea.

48
00:02:13,604 --> 00:02:16,204
From the moment a box comes off one plane

49
00:02:16,204 --> 00:02:18,740
to the moment it's loaded onto the next,

50
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,065
the whole trip through this building

51
00:02:21,065 --> 00:02:22,472
takes well under an hour.

52
00:02:25,422 --> 00:02:27,318
And it isn't only machines.

53
00:02:28,218 --> 00:02:30,593
Around twenty thousand people work

54
00:02:30,593 --> 00:02:32,130
for UPS in Louisville,

55
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:34,016
and the night is when this

56
00:02:34,016 --> 00:02:35,358
place needs them most.

57
00:02:36,408 --> 00:02:38,280
Some of them are students.

58
00:02:39,758 --> 00:02:42,011
Through a program called Metropolitan

59
00:02:42,011 --> 00:02:44,569
College, people working the overnight Next

60
00:02:44,569 --> 00:02:47,126
Day Air shift can have their tuition paid.

61
00:02:48,026 --> 00:02:50,033
They study by day and sort the

62
00:02:50,033 --> 00:02:51,170
country by night.

63
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:54,622
Then everything happens in reverse.

64
00:02:55,522 --> 00:02:57,551
Boxes slide down chutes into

65
00:02:57,551 --> 00:02:59,290
containers for one city.

66
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:01,894
Each container is weighed,

67
00:03:02,194 --> 00:03:04,138
so the plane stays balanced,

68
00:03:04,288 --> 00:03:06,160
and locked into place.
